.Dd October 29, 2026
.Dt DISKLABEL 8
.Os Minkar
.Sh NAME
.Nm disklabel
.Nd manipulate Apple labels
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Fl create Ar device
.Op Fl msize Ns = Ns Ar size
.Op Ar property Ns = Ns Ar value ...
.Nm
.Fl properties Ar device
.Op Ar property Ns Op = Ns Ar value ...
.Nm
.Fl status Ar device
.Sh DESCRIPTION
An Apple label is a 512-byte header at the start of a device and a
property area after it: a property list whose integrity a CRC-32 in the
header guards.
On a partition of type Apple_Label (GUID
.Li 4C616265-6C00-11AA-AA11-00306543ECAC )
the kernel reads the label and publishes the labeled content as a child
medium
.Pq Ar device Ns Li s1 ,
from the label's
.Li Base
(where the content starts, in bytes) and
.Li Size
properties.
The other properties (such as
.Li owner-uid , owner-gid , owner-mode
or
.Li dev-name )
are the label's own.
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl create Ar device
Write a new label: the property area of
.Ar size
bytes (64 KB by default, at most 128 KB; a
.Li k
suffix counts kilobytes) right after the header, the content starting at
the next 4 KB boundary after it and taking the rest of the device, and the
properties given.
.It Fl properties Ar device
Show the properties, or those named; a
.Ar property Ns = Ns Ar value
changes one.
.Li Base
and
.Li Size
are the label's own and are not changed this way.
.It Fl status Ar device
Check the label (magic, version, bounds and checksum) and show it.
.El
.Pp
A value that is a number (with
.Li 0x
for hexadecimal, a leading
.Li 0
for octal, as modes are written) is kept as a number,
.Li true
and
.Li false
as booleans, anything else as a string.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr newfs_hfs 8
